XDJ-RX patch 07 -- multi-field sub-ucom holds + Phase 1 control socket.

Up to MAXHOLD simultaneous persistent A/B holds parsed from every line of the
control snapshot (complementary two-field faders -- e.g. the tempo fader = 0x04
negative half + 0x0a positive half -- must set both at once; with only one field
forced rbp reads the pot as fully pegged).

Phase 1 (standalone-app roadmap) moves the SOURCE of that snapshot off the
per-frame /tmp file poll: when a QEMU chardev id=xdjctrl is present the harness
reads NUL-terminated snapshots from it (QEMU is the socket server; the panel /
Tauri host connects and writes the ENTIRE desired state per record, so one record
== one atomic ctrl-file write). When it is absent the harness falls back to
XDJ_CTRL_PATH (default /tmp/subucom_ctrl), which also makes the file path
per-instance. The text spec and all parsing are unchanged -- only the byte source
moved (xdj_parse_ctrl is the extracted, shared parser). The shared chardev receive
also serves the main-ucom key channel (patch 09, id=xdjkey). chardev frontend
handlers and the SPI-flush frame hook both run under the BQL, so the shared static
buffers need no locking.

